---
title: Federated Login (Google / GitHub / Microsoft)
---
%% OAuth2 sign-in. The app never sees the user's provider password; what it gets back is an
%% identity it maps onto its own user, then mints its OWN JWTs for — federation is the front
%% door only, never the session mechanism.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>LoginComponent
    participant SEC as Spring Security<br/>OAuth2 client
    participant IDP as Provider<br/>Google / GitHub / Microsoft
    participant SH as OAuth2LoginSuccessHandler
    participant FLC as FederatedLoginCompletionService
    participant SESS as SessionService
    participant DB as MySQL

    note over SPA, IDP: Buttons render only for providers whose CLIENT_ID is set —<br/>the SPA discovers them via GET /oauth2/providers.

    U->>SPA: Click "Continue with Google"
    SPA->>SEC: Full-window redirect to<br/>/oauth2/authorization/{provider}
    SEC->>IDP: Authorization request (+ state, PKCE)
    IDP->>U: Consent screen
    U->>IDP: Approve
    IDP->>SEC: Redirect /login/oauth2/code/{provider}?code=…
    SEC->>IDP: Exchange code for tokens (client_secret_post)
    IDP-->>SEC: id_token / userinfo
    SEC->>SH: onAuthenticationSuccess

    SH->>FLC: complete(provider, email, name, request, response)
    note right of FLC: Extracted so OIDC and SAML share one<br/>tail instead of duplicating it.

    FLC->>DB: Find user by email

    alt no account yet
        FLC->>DB: Create FEDERATED user (enabled, no password)
        FLC->>DB: Auto-join organization by email domain
    else existing account
        FLC->>DB: Link this provider to the account
    end

    alt account disabled or locked
        FLC-->>U: Redirect {UI_APP_URL}/login?error=account
    else 2FA enrolled
        FLC-->>U: Redirect /oauth2/callback#mfa=totp — no tokens yet
        note right of FLC: Federation does not bypass 2FA.
    else clear
        FLC->>SESS: issueTokenPair(...)
        SESS->>DB: INSERT refreshsessions (new family)
        FLC-->>U: Redirect /oauth2/callback#access_token=…&refresh_token=…
    end

    U->>SPA: Lands on /oauth2/callback
    SPA->>SPA: Read fragment, persist tokens, clear the URL
    SPA->>U: Navigate to dashboard

    note over SPA, DB: From here the session is indistinguishable from a password login —<br/>same JWTs, same rotation, same revocation.
